## Original Content
Le député LFI des Bouches-du-Rhône Sébastien Delogu est visé par une plainte pour outrage par trois policiers qui étaient en opération à proximité de son domicile.

## Summary
Three police officers in Marseille have filed a complaint for outrage against Sébastien Delogu, a deputy from the LFI party. The complaint alleges that the outrage occurred while the officers were on operation near his home.

## Key Points
- Sébastien Delogu, a deputy from LFI in Bouches-du-Rhône, is accused of outrage by three police officers.
- The incident took place during a police operation near Delogu's residence.
- This event underscores tensions between law enforcement and political figures in France.


